{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Ten camels, of the camels</b> — the reason he took ten is that in proportion to the number of his master's camels he was taking one [out of a set], and besides this, one would have sufficed." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that he took ten camels — meaning, many — along the lines of the verse (I Samuel 1:8) ״טוֹב לָךְ מֵעֲשָׂרָה בָּנִים״." "And the verse's saying <b>of his master's camels</b> means: from those specially designated for his needs, the choice ones kept by him, so that they could carry much; and it comes to exclude the other camels that belonged to Abraham, which were included among the general assets." "And the verse's saying <b>and all the best</b> means: the choicest of his master's possessions — gold, precious stones, and pearls. The reason is: if she will not wish to come after him, she will see his master's wealth. Also, if he must obligate himself in a bride-price, he will show that there is ample means to increase the bride-price and gift. And the verse's saying <b>in his hand</b> means: in his hand."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:07.900209426Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}